<span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div><div class=\"math-block\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>σ</mi><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mrow><mo fence=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℓ</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"script\">F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℓ</mi></msub><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"script\">F</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo fence=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_{\\ell+1}=\\sigma\\!\\left(W_\\ell v_\\ell+\\mathcal F^{-1}[K_\\ell\\,\\mathcal Fv_\\ell]\\right).</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6389em;vertical-align:-0.2083em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">ℓ</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2083em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.2141em;vertical-align:-0.35em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">σ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size1\">(</span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">ℓ</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">ℓ</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0993em;\">F</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8641em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">ℓ</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0993em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">ℓ</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size1\">)</span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div><h2 id=\"algorithm\">Algorithm</h2><p>For a PINN, scale coordinates/units, differentiate residuals, specify collocation points and boundary enforcement, and optimize. FNO trains an operator on input/reference-solution pairs and truncates Fourier modes. Cite the PINN and FNO papers as separate proposals.</p><h2 id=\"conditions\">Conditions and pitfalls</h2><p>Small training loss is not a bound on global solution error or conservation. Examine residual imbalance, shocks, stiff scales and out-of-distribution inputs. Transfer between discretizations is not a guarantee of physical correctness at arbitrary resolution.</p><h2 id=\"verification\">What to check</h2><p>Compare against analytic or independently converged conventional solutions. Measure off-training L1/L2/L∞ errors, boundaries, conservation and multiple seeds. Split operator data by independent problems rather than nearby time slices alone, and report distribution-shift tests separately.</p><h2 id=\"selected-original-source-roles\">Selected original sources and the present small examples</h2><p>Selected section 2 of the 2017 PINN Part I preprint distinguishes residual loss from data and boundary losses. Sections 3–4 of FNO version 3 (2021) combine a local linear map, a Fourier integral map and nonlinear activation. The present small Poisson and periodic-heat inputs are separate educational choices. Neither the full 2019 JCP article nor the original large experiments or performance claims are reproduced.</p><h2 id=\"publication-scope\">Publication scope and related entries</h2><p>Links lead to existing educational code and dated verification records. This reading/translation update changes no scientific code or historical measurements and does not claim reproduction of an entire paper.</p><ul><li><a href=\"/numerical-methods-atlas/methods/pinn-operators/?lang=en\">PINNs and neural operators</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sources\">Primary publications, supporting sources and review scope</h2><p>Distinguish original research, later variants, author monographs, pedagogical articles and official references. Bibliographic verification differs from consulting selected passages; neither implies a full-paper audit or numerical reproduction. Access-depth notes accompany each source.</p><ol class=\"reading-sources\"><li id=\"source-raissi2019\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcp.2018.10.045\">M. Raissi and P. Perdikaris and G.E. Karniadakis (2019). Physics-informed neural networks: A deep learning framework for solving forward and inverse problems involving nonlinear partial differential equations</a>. Journal of Computational Physics<p>Research publication: proposal or related formulation · Abstract and bibliography checked · <a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0021999118307125\">Consulted record</a></p><p>Publisher abstract and method framing; no claim to reproduce the paper benchmarks.</p></li><li id=\"source-li2021fno\"><a href=\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=c8P9NQVtmnO\">Zongyi Li and Nikola Kovachki and Kamyar Azizzadenesheli and Burigede Liu and Kaushik Bhattacharya and Andrew Stuart and Anima Anandkumar (2021). Fourier Neural Operator for Parametric Partial Differential Equations</a>. International Conference on Learning Representations<p>Research publication: proposal or related formulation · Abstract and bibliography checked · <a href=\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=c8P9NQVtmnO\">Consulted record</a></p><p>Conference version; the 2020 arXiv preprint is the same work and is not counted again. Conference manuscript abstract/introduction consulted, not numerically reproduced.</p></li><li id=\"source-raissi2017part1-selected\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1711.10561\">M. Raissi, P. Perdikaris and G. E. Karniadakis (2017). Physics Informed Deep Learning (Part I): Data-driven Solutions of Nonlinear Partial Differential Equations</a>. <p>Research preprint, distinct from the journal edition · Selected source passages consulted · <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1711.10561\">Consulted record</a></p><p>Extracted PDF text selected pp.4–6, §2 continuous-time residual, Eq(2)–(4), Burgers setup and loss/optimizer discussion; not all 22 pages and not visual PDF audit.</p></li><li id=\"source-li2021fno-v3-selected\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2010.08895v3\">Z. Li et al. (2021). Fourier Neural Operator for Parametric Partial Differential Equations</a>. <p>Research preprint, distinct from the journal edition · Selected source passages consulted · <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2010.08895v3\">Consulted record</a></p><p>Selected HTML §2 learning operators; §3 Eq(2); §4 Eq(4)–(5), FFT/truncation/reality; §5 setup and §5.1 Burgers. PDF header/edition only; not full paper or appendix audit.</p></li></ol>",
